+# Browserless UI source reference
+
+**Load when:** an agent has an Angular UI question but no verified browser or geometry snapshot.
+
+```bash
+plw capability describe ui-static --json
+plw ui static "Sign in navigation link" /path/to/angular-project --json
+plw ui static "Sign in" /path/to/angular-project --selector app-layout-header --json
+```
+
+The reference machine reuses the current TS/JS graph and Angular ownership
+sidecar, reads only statically declared template resources, checks their exact
+SHA-256 against the ownership result, then enumerates source text and control
+attributes. Inline literal templates are checked against their source digest.
+The returned `decision` is `RESOLVED` for a unique highest-scoring source
+candidate, `AMBIGUOUS` for tied candidates, or `UNRESOLVED` when nothing
+verified matches. Every candidate names the source owner, template, exact
+digest, source line when external, and query terms that matched. A source
+candidate is never a rendered element identity.
+
+Read `unresolved_templates` and `omitted_candidate_count` before concluding
+anything about absence. A file excluded from a bounded result may still
+contain the relevant UI. A dynamic template or a changed resource remains
+unresolved.
+
+For an edit, inspect the selected template line, declared styles and relevant
+global CSS. Angular control flow such as `@if`, routing, data and responsive
+styles require their own witnesses. The output explicitly marks render
+condition `UNPROVEN` and geometry `UNOBSERVED`. Before claiming overlap or
+visual correctness, capture the exact route, viewport, UI state and fixture
+with an external browser or another trusted geometry host, then use `plw ui
+map` / `plw ui-reference` and runtime provenance as appropriate.
+
+No browser, source mutation, runtime execution, action authority, or task
+postcondition proof is granted by `ui static`.
